      "raw_text": "16   The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus (FTC) tells us that for any polynomial f :\n                                         d\n                                             \u0006\u0005 x          \u0007\n                                        dx     0\n                                                    f(t) dt = f(x)\n                           d\n                               \u0006\u0005 2x 2 \u0007\n     A student calculates dx     x\n                                    t dt as follows:\n                \u0005 2x 2      \u0005 2x 2      \u0005x 2\n         (I)     x\n                    t  dt =  0\n                                t  dt −  0\n                                           t dt\n                         d\n                               \u0006\u0005 x 2 \u0007\n         (II)   By FTC, dx       0\n                                   t dt = x2\n                        d\n                               \u0006\u0005 2x 2 \u0007\n         (III) By FTC, dx        0\n                                    t dt = (2x)2 = 4x2\n                        \u0006\u0005 2x 2 \u0007\n         (IV)       d\n                So dx     x\n                             t dt = 4x2 − x2\n                        d\n                            \u0006\u0005 2x 2 \u0007\n         (V)    giving dx     x\n                                 t dt = 3x2\n     Which of the following best describes the student’s calculation?\n     A The calculation is completely correct.\n     B The calculation is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (I).\n     C The calculation is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (II).\n     D The calculation is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (III).\n     E The calculation is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (IV).\n     F The calculation is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (V).\n                                                    18",
